 "notes": [
  "On 1h, CCI(20) below −100 gave 30,603 entries in 2,522 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.03% ahead of random entries, inside the luck band. The cross back up through −100 fires about four times less often than the level and lands at 0. On 4h and daily, both stay inside the band.",
  "Shorting while CCI(20) was above +100 did 0.25% worse than random entries on 4h and about 4.5% worse on daily. The 4h result comes from 130 entries between Jul 22, 2021 and Sep 9, 2021. The daily one comes from 72 entries between Jan 1, 2021 and May 18, 2021. Without them, both are chance.",
  "SOL daily is the exception. Shorting above +100 did 11% worse than random entries. It stays worse without its strongest stretch and at 10 candles, but not at 50 or 100. On that pair, readings above +100 marked a rally that kept going for a while, not a top.",
  "After CCI(20) crossed up through +100 on daily, price beat random entries by 3.08% and also led at 10 and 50 candles. That gap rests on 8 entries between Jan 1, 2021 and Mar 27, 2021, and SOL's 7.4% comes from the same stretch. Without it, the result is chance. On 1h and 4h the same cross sits inside the band.",
  "Other single stretches fake results too. On 1h, the short on a cross down through +100 led by 0.09%, but only because of 3 entries on May 18–19, 2021, during the May 2021 crash. On SOL 4h, buying below −100 did 0.55% worse, all from 91 entries between Apr 4, 2022 and May 12, 2022, around the Terra collapse.",
  "For a long DCA bot, CCI dips below −100 add nothing on these pairs, so the bot's DCA orders and take profit carry the result. You can leave the condition out, or keep it only as a filter beside conditions you have tested. Where CCI does carry information is on the short side. A short bot that opens while CCI(20) is above +100 on SOL daily is trading against the trend, so that reading is a reason to skip shorts."
